        <data key="d6">cortisol</data><data key="d7">noradrenaline, adrenaline, angiotensin II</data></node><node id="m_nrf2-brake"><data key="d0">nrf2-brake</data><data key="d1">planned</data><data key="d2">7</data><data key="d3">perturbation under noise; induction by noise alone weak</data><data key="d4">the particle resource has this module in three parts already, so the cheapest version is to share it rather than build it: pharmacological NRF2 and HO-1 activation prevents noise-induced endothelial dysfunction, oxidative stress and inflammation. Whether the shared parts take noise unchanged is the test the module cut was designed for.</data><data key="d5">PMID 33921821</data><data key="ng">
            <y:GenericNode configuration="com.yworks.sbgn.Submap">
              <y:Geometry height="90.0" width="240.0" x="520.0" y="375.0"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFFFFF" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="14" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="53.5" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="center" visible="true" width="256.5" x="-8.25" xml:space="preserve" y="18.25" hasText="true">The antioxidant brake:
KEAP1, NRF2 and heme
oxygenase (a removed brake)<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
            </y:GenericNode>
          </data>
        </node><node id="m_redox-nox"><data key="d0">redox-nox</data><data key="d1">redox-nox-v17.graphml</data><data key="ng">
            <y:GenericNode configuration="com.yworks.sbgn.Submap">
              <y:Geometry height="90.0" width="240.0" x="0.0" y="150.0"/>
