              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="14" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="37.0" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="center" visible="true" width="247.0" x="-3.5" xml:space="preserve" y="26.5" hasText="true">NADPH oxidase assembly and
superoxide<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
            </y:GenericNode>
          </data>
        <data key="d6">CYBB, CYBA, NCF1, NCF2, NCF4, RAC1:GTP, Myddosome, NADPH, O2</data><data key="d7">O2.-, NOX2 holoenzyme</data></node><node id="m_redox-sod-h2o2"><data key="d0">redox-sod-h2o2</data><data key="d1">planned</data><data key="d2">2</data><data key="d3">general biochemistry; the arm matters under noise</data><data key="d4">a hole in the map as built, not a new organ: four modules make superoxide and nothing takes it, and the clock module's SOD2 has no substrate. The dismutation in each compartment that makes superoxide, then the peroxide's removal, makes the FOXO3-SOD2 arm do something and gives peroxynitrite a competitor.</data><data key="d5">PMID 16873728, PMID 33921821, PMID 28329261</data><data key="ng">
            <y:GenericNode configuration="com.yworks.sbgn.Submap">
              <y:Geometry height="90.0" width="240.0" x="2080.0" y="450.0"/>
              <y:Fill color="#FFFFFF" transparent="false"/>
              <y:BorderStyle color="#000000" type="line" width="1.0"/>
              <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Dialog" fontSize="14" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="70.0" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="center" visible="true" width="247.0" x="-3.5" xml:space="preserve" y="10.0" hasText="true">Superoxide dismutation and
peroxide handling (SOD1,
SOD2, SOD3, CAT, GPX1,
PRDX3)<y:LabelModel><y:SmartNodeLabelModel distance="4.0"/></y:LabelModel><y:ModelParameter><y:SmartNodeLabelModelParameter labelRatioX="0.0" labelRatioY="0.0" nodeRatioX="0.0" nodeRatioY="0.0" offsetX="0.0" offsetY="0.0" upX="0.0" upY="-1.0"/></y:ModelParameter></y:NodeLabel>
